.TH POSTOUT 1 "July 2026" "Postout 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
postout \- send email through SMTP from scripts, servers, and the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B postout
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B postout config
.RI [ \-\-system ]
.br
.B postout \-\-profile\-list
.br
.B postout \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Postout
is a command-line SMTP mail client designed for scripts, monitoring jobs,
server notifications, and interactive command-line use.
.PP
SMTP settings can be stored in reusable profiles, keeping connection details
and passwords out of shell history and scripts.
.PP
Postout supports personal profiles, shared system profiles, authenticated and
unauthenticated SMTP, SSL/TLS, STARTTLS, plain SMTP, HTML mail, plain-text
mail, multiple recipients, CC, BCC, and file attachments.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B postout config
Open the interactive configuration menu for the current user.
This is the recommended starting point for initial setup, testing, and
personal use.
.TP
.B postout config \-\-system
Open the shared system-profile configuration menu.
Administrator privileges are required.
.PP
System profiles are intended for monitoring jobs, services, scheduled tasks,
and other shared server uses.
.PP
Root can use system profiles immediately.
Other users must be members of the
.B postout
Unix group.
.SH PROFILE SELECTION
A named personal profile takes precedence over a system profile with the same
name.
.PP
When no profile is explicitly selected:
.IP \(bu 2
A single personal profile is selected automatically.
.IP \(bu 2
If no personal profile exists, a single system profile is selected
automatically.
.IP \(bu 2
If multiple available profiles exist, use
.BR \-\-profile .
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " NAME"
Use the named SMTP profile.
.TP
.B \-\-profile\-list
List the SMTP profiles available to the current user.
.TP
.BI \-\-profiles\-file " FILE"
Use an alternative profiles file.
This is an advanced option.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-to " ADDRESS"
Add a primary recipient.
Multiple recipients may be supplied where supported by the command syntax.
.TP
.BI \-\-cc " ADDRESS"
Add a carbon-copy recipient.
.TP
.BI \-\-bcc " ADDRESS"
Add a blind-carbon-copy recipient.
BCC addresses are used for SMTP delivery but are not written into the
message headers.
.TP
.BI \-\-subject " TEXT"
Set the message subject.
.TP
.BI \-\-body " TEXT"
Set the plain-text message body.
.TP
.BI \-\-html " HTML"
Set an HTML message body.
Postout generates a plain-text alternative automatically.
.TP
.BI \-\-attach " FILE"
Attach a regular file to the message.
The combined attachment size is limited by Postout.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display the complete command-line help.
.SH EXAMPLES
Configure a profile for the current user:
.PP
.nf
.RS
postout config
.RE
.fi
.PP
Configure shared profiles for server notifications:
.PP
.nf
.RS
postout config \-\-system
.RE
.fi
.PP
List available profiles:
.PP
.nf
.RS
postout \-\-profile\-list
.RE
.fi
.PP
Send a simple message:
.PP
.nf
.RS
postout \-\-profile work \e
    \-\-to recipient@example.com \e
    \-\-subject "Backup completed" \e
    \-\-body "The nightly backup completed successfully."
.RE
.fi
.PP
Send an HTML message:
.PP
.nf
.RS
postout \-\-profile work \e
    \-\-to recipient@example.com \e
    \-\-subject "Service report" \e
    \-\-html "<h1>Service report</h1><p>All checks passed.</p>"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Send a message with an attachment:
.PP
.nf
.RS
postout \-\-profile work \e
    \-\-to recipient@example.com \e
    \-\-subject "Monthly report" \e
    \-\-body "The monthly report is attached." \e
    \-\-attach report.pdf
.RE
.fi
.PP
Expire cached sudo authentication and test system configuration elevation:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo \-k
postout config \-\-system
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/postout/profiles.json
Personal SMTP profiles.
When
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set, Postout uses
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/postout/profiles.json .
.TP
.I /etc/postout/profiles.json
Shared system SMTP profiles.
.TP
.I /usr/share/postout/
Installed Postout Python package files on Debian-based systems.
.SH SYSTEM PROFILE ACCESS
The
.I /etc/postout
directory and system profiles are protected by filesystem permissions.
.PP
Members of the
.B postout
Unix group can read and use all configured system SMTP profiles, including
their stored SMTP credentials.
.PP
After a user is added to the group, that user may need to log out and back in
before the new group membership becomes active.
.SH SECURITY
Prefer stored profiles over supplying SMTP passwords directly on the command
line.
Command-line arguments may be visible in shell history or process listings.
.PP
Personal profile files should remain readable only by their owner.
System profiles should remain restricted to root and members of the
.B postout
group.
.PP
Postout transmits HTML content as supplied.
Only send trusted HTML.
.PP
For Gmail and other providers that support application-specific passwords,
use an application password rather than the account's primary password.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested operation completed successfully.
.TP
.B non-zero
Configuration, validation, file, SMTP, authentication, permission, or message
delivery failure.
